'''Aku Enemies''' (悪魔 ''Akuma'', '''Devils''' or '''Demons'''), also known as just '''the Aku''', are a type of [[Enemy Units|Enemy Unit]] first introduced in the [[Empress' Research]] stages and [[Uncanny Legends]]. They are the second blue enemy type in the game, though they are a darker shade of blue than [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]], with black accents. Most Aku carry at least one of two exclusive abilities: [[Shield]]s are a [[Barrier]]-like defense that absorbs cumulative damage which regenerates each time their bearer receives a damage-based knockback, and [[Death Surge]] gives its user a chance to produce a [[Surge Attack]] when killed.

Like [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angels]], Aku cannot have the [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] trait, according to the [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Aku Researcher]].

See [[:Category:Anti-Aku Cats|here]] for a list of units with anti-Aku abilities.

*Aku enemies are associated with Aku [[Catfruit]], which is obtainable from [[Growing Evil]] after clearing [[Unleashing the Cats]] (see Growing Evil's article for its schedule).
*Aku [[Talent Orbs]] can be obtained from the following stages:
**[[Enigma Stages]]: [[Cradle Shrine (Deadly)/Aku|Bad Instinct's Origin]], [[Summit Shrine (Merciless)/Aku|Bad Instinct's Apex]], [[Frontier Shrine (Merciless)/Aku|Bad Instinct's Refuge]]
**[[Attack of the Omens]] [[Continuation Stage]]s: [[Attack of the Omens/Cradle Wilderness (Deadly)|Cradle Wilderness]], [[Attack of the Omens/Summit Wilderness (Merciless)|Summit Wilderness]], [[Attack of the Omens/Frontier Wilderness (Merciless)|Frontier Wilderness]]

==Trivia==
*''Aku'' (悪) is a Japanese word meaning "evil" or "wickedness".
*In all main versions of the game except the [[The Battle Cats|English Version]], the Aku trait's name directly translates to "Devil" or "Demon".
**The English localization of 悪魔 ''Akuma'' being Aku rather than Devil/Demon may be to help distinguish these enemies from non-Aku demons such as [[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Lesser Demon Cat]], [[Hannya]], the [[Demon of Deciliter Bay]] and the [[Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Collaboration Event|Demon Slayer Collab]] enemies. In Japanese, such characters are referred to as other words that also tend to be translated as "demon", like 鬼 ''[[wikipedia:Oni|oni]]'' or 魔物 ''mamono'', rather than 悪魔 ''akuma''.
**Strangely, 悪魔 was localized as "Devil" rather than Aku in the English names of [[Devil's Nest (Cat)|Devil's Nest]] and [[The Devil's Rhythm (Merciless)|The Devil's Rhythm]].
**The Japanese name of the ''[[Street Fighter Collaboration Event|Street Fighter]]'' character [[Akuma (Enemy)|Akuma]] is Gōki (豪鬼), hence why he wasn't updated to have the Aku trait.
*There is an inconsistency with the pluralization of Aku. In unit descriptions it's just ''Aku''. but on [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Aku Researcher]]'s sign it's ''Akus''.
*Aku have their own writing system consisting of pixelated upside-down or sideways katakana. This text is not translated between languages.
