*[[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge Cat]]'s staff seems to bear the "evil eye" associated with Aku, though it may just be a reference to ''[[wikipedia:Magical Circle Guru Guru|Magical Circle Guru Guru]]'', as it predates Aku enemies.
*This type may have been inspired by the [https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/t/%a4%c7%a4%b9 Death enemies] from [[Yuru-i GeGeGe no Kitarou: Youkai Dotabata Daisensou|YuruGeGe]], which also looked demonic and had a barrier-like ability that blocked off damage.
**Aku enemies' designs could've also been based off of [[Zombie Cat (Special Cat)|Zombie Cat]]'s Evolved Form, Devil Cat.
*The first Aku enemy is technically [[Dark Emperor Santa]], who was retroactively given the trait in [[Version 11.3 Update|Version 11.3]]. This change was likely made because his Japanese name (悪魔王サンタ ''Akuma Ō Santa'', "Devil King Santa") contains 悪魔 ''Akuma'' ("Devil"), which is also the Japanese name of the Aku trait.
**Dark Emperor Santa is the only Aku to have gained the Aku trait retroactively instead of being Aku from the start, the first Aku to have another trait, and the first Aku who is not predominantly blue. The second is [[Poultrio]].
*Many Aku enemies' Japanese names contain the English word ''devil'' written in katakana. [[Aku Doge]], [[Aku Cyclone]], [[Ackey]] and [[Miz Devil]] have デビル ''Debiru'', while [[Devil Wife]] strangely has デヴィル ''Deviru''. Devil Wife's unusual spelling is most likely a pun: her full name (デヴィル夫人 ''Deviru Fujin'', "Lady Devil") is nearly identical to a common nickname for TV personality [[wikipedia:Dewi Sukarno|Dewi Sukarno]] (デヴィ夫人 ''Devi Fujin'', "Lady Dewi"), who also donates to the poor.
*Some Aku enemies and various [[Cat Units]] have descriptions pertaining to how they came to be after making a devilish deal:
**[[Cerberus Kids]] simply joined their ranks after accepting an Aku recruitment advertisement.
**[[Condemned Peng]]'s pact with the Aku gave him a body that needs no rest so he could reprise his role from "The Sleepless Peng" for its sequel, as well as a beam he can fire from his head.
**[[Le'Behemoth]] sold his soul for "a set of very hard to come by photos" for his collection, which he protects with a Shield.
**[[Ackey]] sold his twin brother's soul to win a baseball tournament.
**[[Vermilingua Rangmaster]] made an Aku contract for x-ray vision, ostensibly to better sculpt nude statue subjects, but it only enabled him to see skeletons.
**[[Hevijak the Wicked (Uber Rare Cat)|Hevijak]] made an Aku contract in exchange for raw destructive power.
**[[Summoner Satoru (Uber Rare Cat)|Satoru]] signed an Aku contract for the greater good by manipulating his summons with his sense of justice.
*[[Aku Gory]] is the only Aku enemy to appear in a [[Main Chapters Levels|Main Chapter]] other than The Aku Realms, appearing in [[Cats of the Cosmos]] Chapter 3 [[Gorigori (Cats of the Cosmos)/Outbreak|Gorigori]]'s [[Zombie Outbreaks|Zombie Outbreak]].
*Despite being introduced later than the [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] trait, Aku was listed before Relic in all menus such as the [[Upgrade Menu]] until [[Version 13.3 Update|Version 13.3]].
*Aku, Relic and [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] are the only standard enemy types without [[Fruit Treasures]].

